her road user and no device is in the scene."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car drives past the fire hydrant at 6 m/s, its body 1.5 m from it, without halting."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts parallel to the curb with its body 10 m from the nearest hydrant, where no angle-parking or no-parking sign or zone applies: beyond fifteen feet."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A car halts near a fire hydrant, but the source maps regions without outlines (st.region_geometry absent): its distance to the hydrant is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts in an angled bay (angle 60 degrees) with its body 5.5 m from a fire hydrant: beyond fifteen feet but within twenty, the bound of an angle-parking location."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts parallel to the curb with its body 5.5 m from a hydrant where no angle-parking or no-parking sign or zone applies: beyond fifteen feet."}],"literals":[{"span":"h5","text":"fifteen feet","value":15,"unit":"ft"},{"span":"h6","text":"twenty feet","value":20,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of object-tracking and vehicle-dynamics recordings"},{"name":"p.queue_halt_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue","source":"queue spacing (jam density) of urban traffic-flow studies"},{"name":"p.parking_space_angle_resolution","unit":"deg","value":5.0,"convention":"the bay angle at or below which a mapped parking bay counts as parallel to the curb rather than angled: the source's angle resolution for mapped bays","source":"angle resolution of the source's map annotation"}],"gaps":[{"span":"p4","kind":"operator","proposal":"`Formula.requiredByRuleSet (who : Arg)`: true at an observation where some rule of the set, engaged there for road user `who`, requires of it the conduct it shows there (here a halt), so that the conduct is in compliance with law; false where no engaged rule requires it; unknown where an engaged rule's requirement is unknown. It decides whether a halt is one another law requires (yielding to a pedestrian, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, at a railway crossing), which the words except from the prohibition.","nearest":"Formula.rule and Formula.ruleApplies compose one named rule and read its verdict or its engagement: neither ranges over the rules of the set nor says that a rule requires the conduct shown; the device atoms (dev.stop_sign, dev.traffic_signal, dev.governs) carry only the halts a device directs."}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_52_130_A5","law_refs":["LVMC-11-52-130-A5"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"p1","text":"No person shall stop, stand or park a vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"p2","text":"except when necessary to avoid conflict","role":"standard"},{"id":"p3","text":"with other traffic","role":"exception"},{"id":"p4","text":"in compliance with law","role":"exception"},{"id":"p5","text":"or the directions of a police officer","role":"exception"},{"id":"p6","text":"or a traffic control device,","role":"exception"},{"id":"p7","text":"in any of the following places:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"e1","text":"In front of any sidewalk elevator or chute","role":"condition"},{"id":"e2","text":"or within a space of five feet on each side of such sidewalk elevator or chute.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"p1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"\"stop\" here is prohibited, so DEF-NRS-484A-260 applies by its own scope (\"when prohibited, any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\"); standing and parking are halts too, so the three together are any halt: drv.motion.complete_halt (\"The road user is at rest at the observation\"), a state at one observation, not an act over time. \"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole. \"No person\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"p3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"other traffic\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel\"), claimed whole for a road user other than the subject; rel.ahead_behind_in_lane (\"a is ahead of / behind b in the same 