cer."},{"span":"p6","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.traffic_signal","dev.railway_signal_or_gate","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the directions of ... a traffic control device\" to halt: a stop sign (dev.stop_sign, \"regulatory sign requiring a full halt\"), a yield sign (dev.yield_sign), a traffic signal (dev.traffic_signal) showing circular_red, a red_arrow, flashing_red or circular_yellow, or a railway signal or gate (dev.railway_signal_or_gate) with lights flashing or gate not up, governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). Each device is read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"d1","atoms":["st.driveway_or_alley_entrance","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only: \"driveway\" (DEF-NRS-484A-190, \"every way or place in private ownership and used for vehicular travel by the owner and those having express or implied permission\"), public or private, where it meets the street, is nearest to st.driveway_or_alley_entrance (\"private road, alley or driveway meeting the highway\"), whose not-a-stand-in clause says \"the kind does not tell an alley's entrance from a private road's or driveway's\": the forbidden place would be read at every alley entrance too. \"In front of or within five feet of\" is the ground distance from the body (st.region_geometry, \"zero when they overlap\") at most the stated figure. The span is a gap."},{"span":"d2","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.parked"],"justification":"\"the parking of a vehicle\": \"parking\" is DEF-NRS-484A-155 (\"the standing of a vehicle, whether occupied or not, otherwise than temporarily for the purpose of and while actually engaged in loading or unloading\"), drv.motion.parked (\"Road user a is parked: \\\"the standing of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\\\"\") with p.parking_min_duration; \"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate, claimed whole. The exception covers parking only, not a brief stop."},{"span":"d4","atoms":["st.driveway_or_alley_entrance"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atom only: the driveway region is st.driveway_or_alley_entrance, but no atom records who owns or controls a driveway or whether the person parking is that person, a family member or an invitee; the span is a gap."},{"span":"d5","atoms":["ru.official_vehicle"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atom only: ru.official_vehicle (\"a vehicle in official or contracted road service, identifiable by livery or equipment; kind ∈ {tow, utility, ..., municipal, other}\") has no postal kind; kind other does not tell a United States Postal Service vehicle from any other official vehicle. The reference to Paragraph (1) concerns another line of the same section; this node carries the exception for Paragraph (7). The span is a gap."},{"span":"d6","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"\"while it is being operated on official business\" is a purpose: read through the conduct it explains, the postal vehicle's halt at the place (drv.motion.complete_halt, \"The road user is at rest at the observation\"), taken as a halt in the course of its business; disclosed as an observable reading of category purpose."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false},{"span":"d3","standard":"in or near a private driveway","concepts":["st.driveway_or_alley_entrance","st.region_geometry"],"params":["p.driveway_near_reach"],"convention":"one passenger-car length of frontage: a vehicle parked with its body within that ground distance of the driveway is parked near it","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), has its body in front of or within five feet (literal 5 ft) of a public or private driveway: for a driveway entrance e (gap: no atom tells a driveway's entrance from an alley's; nearest st.driveway_or_alley_entrance), st_region_geometry_distance(subject, e) is at most five feet. None of the exceptions holds at the observation: no road user o of traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, not the subject) is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a body gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; no police officer's direction to stop (dev.human_direction role police_officer, indication stop) governs a travel region the subject occupies; no stop sign, yield sign, traffic signal showing a red or yellow indication, or flashing railway signal or lowered gate governs (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region); the halt is not one another law requires (gap on span p4); it is not the parking (drv.motion.parked with p.halt_speed_tolerance and p.parking_min_duration), within p.driveway_near_reach of a private driveway, of a vehicle controlled by the driveway's owner or controller or a family member or invitee (gap on span d4); and the subject is not a United States Postal Service vehicle halted on its business (gap on span d5).","obligation":"The subject is not at rest: drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold at the observation.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.queue_halt_gap","p.parking_min_duration","p.driveway_near_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"p2","why":"\"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic\" is read only through a road user of traffic ahead of the vehicle in its lane within the queue gap; a halt for crossing traffic that is not ahead in the lane is not read as necessary.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"d6","why":"\"being operated on official business\" is a purpose read through the postal vehicle's halt at the place itself: every halt of such a vehicle there is taken as made on its business.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"purpose"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts across the mouth of a residential driveway, its body overlapping the entrance, with no road user ahead and no device or officer governing its lane, and stays at rest; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car drives past the driveway at 8 m/s without halting."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts at the curb 15 m from the nearest driveway."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A car halts near a driveway, but the source maps regions without outlines (st.region_geometry absent): whether it is within five feet is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts 1 m from a driveway behind a car halted 2 m ahead of it in the same lane: a halt in a queue of traffic."}],"literals":[{"span":"d1","text":"five feet","value":5,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of object-tracking and vehicle-dynamics recordings"},{"name":"p.queue_halt_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue","source":"queue spacing (jam density) of urban traffic-flow studies"},{"name":"p.parking_min_duration","unit":"s","value":180.0,"convention":"the longest halt counted as temporary, as for loading or unloading: a common time limit of a passenger loading zone","source":"municipal passenger loading zone time limits"},{"name":"p.driveway_near_reach","unit":"m","value":6.0,"convention":"the ground distance from a parked vehicle's body to a private driveway within which it is parked near that driveway: about one passenger-car length of the frontage the driveway serves","source":"passenger-car design vehicle length (AASHTO P vehicle, about 5.8 m)"}],"gaps":[{"span":"p4","kind":"operator","proposal":"`Formula.requiredByRuleSet (who : Arg)`: true at an observation where some rule of the set, engaged there for road user `who`, requires of it the conduct it shows there (here a halt), so that the conduct is in compliance with law; false where no engaged rule requires it; unknown where an engaged rule's requirement is unknown. It decides whether a halt is one another law requires (yielding to a pedestrian, stopping before the sidewalk on emerging from a driveway, for a school bus or an emergency vehicle), which the words except from the prohibition.","nearest":"Formula.rule and Formula.ruleApplies compose one named rule and read its verdict or its engagement: neither ranges over the rules of the set nor says that a rule requires the conduct shown; the device atoms (dev.stop_sign, dev.traffic_signal, dev.governs) carry only the halts a device directs."},{"span":"d1","kind":"atom","proposal":"`st.driveway_entrance` | the place where a driveway, a way used for vehicular travel to a property (in private ownership or public), meets the highway, carried as a region with a reference point and a boundary **Not a stand-in for:** an alley's entrance or a private road's | general. It decides where a halt is forbidden: in front of or within the stated distance of a driveway, and not of an alley.","nearest":"st.driveway_or_alley_entrance: its not-a-stand-in clause states that the kind does not tell an alley's entrance from a private road's or driveway's, so the forbidden place would be read at every alley entrance."},{"span":"d4","kind":"atom","proposal":"`rel.premises_privilege` | relation: the road user's vehicle is controlled by the person who owns or is in control of a private driveway region, or by a family member or invitee of that person, as the source records it **Not a stand-in for:** the vehicle's owner (DEF-NRS-484A-150) or its position | local. It decides whose parking at the driveway the words exempt.","nearest":"st.driveway_or_alley_entrance carries the driveway's place only; no atom records who owns or controls it or the relation of the person parking to that person."},{"span":"d5","kind":"atom","proposal":"`ru.postal_vehicle` | a vehicle of the national postal service, identifiable by its livery **Not a stand-in for:** an official vehicle of another service (`ru.official_vehicle`) | local. It decides which road users the words exempt.","nearest":"ru.official_vehicle: its kinds (tow, utility, highway_maintenance, incident_management, regulatory_agency, coroner, armored_car, municipal, other) carry no postal kind, and kind other does not tell a postal vehicle from any other."}],"gap_resolutions":[]}

