{"node_id":"LVMC_11_52_060","law_refs":["LVMC-11-52-060"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","ru.aggregate=DEF-LVMC-11-02-170::trailer"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"s1","text":"In no case shall any part of any vehicle","role":"subject"},{"id":"s2","text":"part of the load of such vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s3","text":"or trailer","role":"subject"},{"id":"s4","text":"attached to such vehicle","role":"condition"},{"id":"s5","text":"project","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s6","text":"into the street","role":"condition"},{"id":"s7","text":"more than fifteen feet","role":"obligation"},{"id":"s8","text":"measured on a line at right angles to the curb.","role":"obligation"}],"elements":[{"span":"s1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","kin.extent"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"any vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle (\"every device in, upon or by which any person or property is or may be transported or drawn upon a highway\"), claimed whole and never expanded into classes. \"any part of\" the vehicle is any point of its body, whose size kin.extent carries (\"the body's size along its axes about the reference point\"), so the farthest point of the body is what the bound reads. \"In no case\" admits no exception."},{"span":"s3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-LVMC-11-02-170::trailer"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"trailer\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-LVMC-11-02-170::trailer (\"a vehicle, other than a commercial vehicle or recreational vehicle, that is without motor power, is designed and constructed to be drawn by a motor vehicle\"), claimed whole: the trailer is judged as a road user of its own, its body read by the same bound."},{"span":"s5","atoms":[],"derived":["drv.motion.parked"],"justification":"\"project\" states where a standing body stands out into the street, in a section of the chapter on stopping, standing and parking: it is read for a vehicle that stands in the street, drv.motion.parked (\"Road user a is parked: \\\"the standing of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\\\", observed as a at rest at every observation of the window behind the observation\"). A moving vehicle travelling in a lane farther from the curb than the bound is not projecting from the curb; the narrowing on this span discloses the reading."},{"span":"s6","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.highway"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"street\" is DEF-NRS-484A-265 (\"the entire width between the boundary lines of every highway inside the territorial limits of a city\", not an aggregate): st.highway (\"the entire public way between its boundary lines, including sidewalks and shoulders\"); its \"not a stand-in for: the roadway\" clause is respected since the definition names the entire width, not the roadway. rel.occupies (\"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region\") anchors the vehicle on its own street. The city limits are the ordinance's own territorial scope, the map the reading applies the city code to, as for every other \"street\" of this code (mapping index: \"upon a street\" -> rel.occupies, st.highway)."},{"span":"s7","atoms":["st.region_geometry","kin.extent"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"more than fifteen feet\" is the stated figure (literal): the body's projection, the ground distance from the curb to its outline (st.region_geometry, \"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it\") plus the body's own extent across the curb line (kin.extent, \"a formula reads the full length, width and height\"), is compared with it; a projection at most the figure complies."},{"span":"s8","atoms":["st.road_edge","st.region_geometry","st.on_way","st.highway","kin.heading","kin.extent","st.lane_direction","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the curb\" is st.road_edge (\"curb or edge of the roadway\") lying on the vehicle's street (st.on_way, \"the public way (a highway region) a structure region lies on\"); the curb the vehicle stands at is the road edge of that street nearest its body (st.region_geometry ground distance). \"on a line at right angles to the curb\": the curb runs along the designated direction of the travel region the vehicle occupies (st.lane_direction, \"direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in ... a roadway\"; rel.occupies; st.travel_region), so the body's extent at right angles to the curb is its length (kin.extent) times the absolute cross product of its heading (kin.heading, read normalised) with that direction plus its width times their absolute dot product. The sign of the direction does not matter. st.lane_direction is not used as a manoeuvre or a path: only its line is read; the narrowing on this span discloses the reading."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"s2","why":"A load overhanging the body is not observed: kin.extent is the body's size, and no atom carries a load standing out beyond it. The rule judges the body (and a trailer as its own body); a projection made only by an overhanging load is not captured."},{"span":"s4","why":"A trailer is itself \"a vehicle\" by its definition DEF-LVMC-11-02-170, so the duty binds its body through \"any vehicle\" whether or not it is attached; attachment adds no restriction.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle","ru.aggregate=DEF-LVMC-11-02-170::trailer"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle or a trailer (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle or DEF-LVMC-11-02-170::trailer), is parked at the observation (drv.motion.parked(subject; speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance, min_duration = p.parking_min_duration)) and its footprint overlaps a highway h (rel.occupies subject h, st.highway): it stands in a street.","obligation":"For every highway h the subject occupies (rel.occupies), every road edge c (st.road_edge) lying on h (st.on_way c h) whose ground distance from the subject's body (st_region_geometry_distance) is at most that of every other road edge lying on h (the curb the vehicle stands at), and every travel region r (st.travel_region) the subject occupies (rel.occupies): the ground distance from the subject's body to c, plus the subject's length (kin_extent length) times the absolute value of the cross product of its heading (kin_heading x, y) with r's designated direction (st_lane_direction x, y), plus its width (kin_extent width) times the absolute value of their dot product, is at most fifteen feet (literal 15 ft). Where r carries no direction, the heading or the geometry is unobserved, the sum is unknown.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.parking_min_duration"],"narrowings":[{"span":"s5","why":"\"project\" is read for a vehicle that stands in the street, parked (at rest for p.parking_min_duration): a vehicle travelling or halted briefly in traffic is not judged, though the words name no state of motion; the section sits among the stopping, standing and parking rules and measures from the curb a vehicle stands at.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"s8","why":"The curb's line is read as the designated direction of the travel region the vehicle occupies, and the curb as the road edge of its street nearest its body; the projection is the body-to-curb distance plus the body's extent across that line, which assumes the body lies on the street side of the curb.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A truck 10 m long is parked for 10 minutes at right angles to the curb of a two-lane street, 0.2 m from the curb; its heading is perpendicular to the roadway's direction, so its body reaches about 10.2 m into the street, beyond fifteen feet."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A passenger car 1.8 m wide is parked for 10 minutes parallel to the curb, 0.3 m from it, heading along the roadway's direction: its body reaches about 2.1 m into the street."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car travels at 12 m/s along the far lane of the street, 8 m from the curb: it is not parked, so the rule does not apply."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A truck is parked at right angles to the curb, but the source maps regions without their outline (st.region_geometry absent): the distance from the body to the curb is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"A detached trailer 8 m long is parked for 10 minutes at right angles to the curb, 0.1 m from it: as a vehicle in its own right its body reaches about 8.1 m into the street."}],"literals":[{"span":"s7","text":"fifteen feet","value":15,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of object-tracking and vehicle-dynamics recordings"},{"name":"p.parking_min_duration","unit":"s","value":180.0,"convention":"the longest halt counted as temporary, as for loading or unloading: a common time limit of a passenger loading zone","source":"municipal passenger loading zone time limits"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_52_070","law_refs":["LVMC-11-52-070"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"t1","text":"The City Traffic Engineer shall determine upon what streets angle parking shall be permitted,","role":"condition"},{"id":"t2","text":"and shall provide signage or other markings to indicate where such parking is permitted.","role":"condition"},{"id":"t3","text":"Where angle parking is permitted,","role":"condition"},{"id":"t4","text":"no person shall stand or park a vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"t5","text":"unless the front of the vehicle is pointed toward the direction of lawful traffic movement.","role":"obligation"}],"elements":[{"span":"t1","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","st.parking_space","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"The Traffic Engineer's determination of the streets where angle parking is permitted is a legal status no scene shows; the next words name its evidence, the signage or markings. It is read through them: a regulatory sign of code angle_parking (dev.regulatory_sign, \"a point regulation by catalogue code ... angle_parking\") governing (dev.governs, \"the travel regions whose traffic the device controls\") the travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region), or a marked parking bay (st.parking_space, \"marked bay for standing or parking; angle attribute\") whose angle stands clear of zero. The sign is a condition, not a manoeuvre (its not-a-stand-in clause)."},{"span":"t2","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","st.parking_space","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"signage\" is the angle_parking regulatory sign (dev.regulatory_sign) governing (dev.governs) the travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region); \"other markings\" is a marked bay (st.parking_space, \"marked bay for standing or parking; angle attribute\") the vehicle occupies whose angle (st_parking_space_angle) stands clear of zero by more than the source's angle resolution. Their presence is the evidence of the permission they indicate."},{"span":"t3","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","st.parking_space","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"Where angle parking is permitted\" is the place the signage or markings indicate: a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region) that an angle_parking sign governs (dev.regulatory_sign, dev.governs), or that the vehicle occupies together with an angled marked bay (st.parking_space with its angle clear of zero). Presence of the feature, no size bound: the angle is read only against the source's resolution."},{"span":"t4","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.parked"],"justification":"Same words and meaning as the mapping index's \"No person shall stand or park a vehicle\" (LVMC_11_52_040_A): drv.motion.parked (\"Road user a is parked: \\\"the standing of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\\\"\") with the standing duration as its window, covering standing (DEF-NRS-484A-250, \"the halting of a vehicle ... otherwise than for the purpose of and while actually engaged in receiving or discharging passengers\") and parking (DEF-NRS-484A-155); \"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole. \"No person\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"t5","atoms":["kin.heading","st.lane_direction","rel.occupies","st.travel_region","ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic"],"derived":[],"justification":"Same words as the mapping index's \"headed in the direction of lawful traffic movement\" (LVMC_11_52_040_A): \"the front of the vehicle\" points along kin.heading (\"direction the body points\"; not its velocity, so a standing vehicle has one); \"the direction of lawful traffic movement\" is the direction designated for traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, claimed whole as the word's admitted aggregate) on the travel region the vehicle occupies: st.lane_direction (\"direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in\"), read on that region (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). \"pointed toward\" is a positive dot product of the heading with that direction."}],"operationalizations":[],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), occupies (rel.occupies) a travel region r (st.travel_region) where angle parking is permitted: a regulatory sign of code angle_parking (dev.regulatory_sign) governs r (dev.governs), or the subject also occupies a parking space (st.parking_space) whose angle (st_parking_space_angle), in absolute value, exceeds p.parking_space_angle_resolution.","obligation":"Where the subject is parked (drv.motion.parked(subject; speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance, min_duration = p.standing_min_duration)), for every travel region r it occupies that is selected as in the applicability (governed by an angle_parking sign, or occupied together with an angled parking space), the dot product of the subject's heading (kin_heading) with r's designated direction (st_lane_direction) is positive: the front of the vehicle points toward the direction of lawful traffic movement. A subject that is not parked complies. Where r carries no direction or the heading is unobserved, the verdict is unknown.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.standing_min_duration","p.parking_space_angle_resolution"],"narrowings":[{"span":"t1","why":"The Traffic Engineer's determination is a legal status read through the signage or markings that display it: a determination no sign or marking displays is not read.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"t2","why":"The duty to provide signage or markings is the Engineer's and is not judged on a trace; the presence of the angle_parking sign or the angled marked bay is read as the indication of where angle parking is permitted.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"},{"span":"t5","why":"\"the direction of lawful traffic movement\" is read as the designated direction of the travel region the vehicle occupies at the angle-parking place; a vehicle wholly inside a bay that overlaps no travel region is not judged.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car has backed into an angled bay (angle 45 degrees) on a street whose lane carries an angle_parking sign; its rear overlaps the lane and its heading is opposite the lane's direction; it stays at rest for 5 minutes."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car stands for 5 minutes in the same angled bay with its heading 45 degrees off the lane's direction, pointing forward with traffic: the dot product with the lane's direction is positive."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car is parked parallel to the curb on a street with no angle_parking sign and no angled bay: the rule does not apply."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A car is parked in an angled bay at an angle_parking sign, but the source does not supply headings (kin.heading absent): where its front points is unknown.","masked":["kin.heading"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car pulls into the angled bay heading against the lane's direction, halts 20 seconds to let a passenger out and leaves: it neither stands nor parks for the standing duration."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of object-tracking and vehicle-dynamics recordings"},{"name":"p.standing_min_duration","unit":"s","value":60.0,"convention":"the longest halt counted as receiving or discharging passengers or loading rather than standing: a passenger pick-up dwell at the curb","source":"curbside passenger pick-up dwell-time studies"},{"name":"p.parking_space_angle_resolution","unit":"deg","value":5.0,"convention":"the bay angle at or below which a mapped parking bay counts as parallel to the curb rather than angled: the source's angle resolution for mapped bays","source":"angle resolution of the source's map annotation"}],"gaps":[],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_52_130_A11","law_refs":["LVMC-11-52-130-A11"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"p1","text":"No person shall stop, stand or park a vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"p2","text":"except when necessary to avoid conflict","role":"standard"},{"id":"p3","text":"with other traffic","role":"exception"},{"id":"p4","text":"in compliance with law","role":"exception"},{"id":"p5","text":"or the directions of a police officer","role":"exception"},{"id":"p6","text":"or a traffic control device,","role":"exception"},{"id":"p7","text":"in any of the following places:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"a1","text":"Within fifteen feet of an intersection.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"p1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"\"stop\" here is prohibited, so DEF-NRS-484A-260 applies by its own scope (\"when prohibited, any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\"); standing and parking are halts too, so the three together are any halt: drv.motion.complete_halt (\"The road user is at rest at the observation\"), a state at one observation, not an act over time. \"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole. \"No person\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"p3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"other traffic\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel\"), claimed whole for a road user other than the subject; rel.ahead_behind_in_lane (\"a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane, along the lane direction\") places it ahead of the halted vehicle and rel.surface_gap (\"distance between the nearest points of two bodies\") measures the gap the operationalization bounds; a centre distance would overstate it (rel.centre_distance's not-a-stand-in clause)."},{"span":"p4","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.stop_sign","dev.traffic_signal","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only: the device atoms carry the halts a device directs (read on span p6), not a halt that another law requires of the vehicle (yielding to a pedestrian, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, at a railway crossing); no atom or operator decides that some engaged rule requires the halt the vehicle makes. The span is a gap."},{"span":"p5","atoms":["dev.human_direction","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Same mapping as the index's \"unless otherwise directed by a Police Officer\": dev.human_direction (\"a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ∈ {police_officer, ...}; indication ∈ {stop, proceed, slow, turn(dir)}\") with role police_officer and indication stop, governing (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies). dev.governs is read as control of that region, not as the place of the halt (its not-a-stand-in clause). \"police officer\" (DEF-NRS-484A-180) is the role police_officer."},{"span":"p6","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.traffic_signal","dev.railway_signal_or_gate","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the directions of ... a traffic control device\" to halt: a stop sign (dev.stop_sign, \"regulatory sign requiring a full halt\"), a yield sign (dev.yield_sign), a traffic signal (dev.traffic_signal) showing circular_red, a red_arrow, flashing_red or circular_yellow, or a railway signal or gate (dev.railway_signal_or_gate) with lights flashing or gate not up, governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). Each device is read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"a1","atoms":["st.intersection","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"an intersection\" (DEF-NRS-484A-105, \"the area embraced within the prolongation or connection of the lateral curb lines ... of the roadways of two highways\"; an alley junction is none) is st.intersection (\"the region where two roadways meet, bounded by the prolongation of their edges; a junction where an alley meets another way ... is no intersection\"). \"Within fifteen feet of\" is the ground distance from the vehicle's body to it, st.region_geometry (\"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)\"), which anchors the vehicle; occupancy is not read (its not-a-stand-in clause) since the words state a distance."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), has its body within fifteen feet (literal 15 ft) of an intersection: some st.intersection region i with st_region_geometry_distance(subject, i) at most fifteen feet. None of the exceptions holds at the observation: no road user o of traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, not the subject) is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a body gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; no police officer's direction to stop (dev.human_direction role police_officer, indication stop) governs a travel region the subject occupies; no stop sign, yield sign, traffic signal showing a red or yellow indication, or flashing railway signal or lowered gate governs (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region); and the halt is not one another law requires (gap on span p4).","obligation":"The subject is not at rest: drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold at the observation.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.queue_halt_gap"],"narrowings":[{"span":"p2","why":"\"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic\" is read only through a road user of traffic ahead of the vehicle in its lane within the queue gap; a halt for crossing traffic that is not ahead in the lane is not read as necessary.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts 2 m short of an intersection's edge with no road user ahead of it, no officer and no device governing its lane, and stays at rest; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car drives through the stretch 2 m short of the intersection at 8 m/s without halting."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts 40 m from the nearest intersection."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A car halts near an intersection, but the source maps regions without outlines (st.region_geometry absent): whether it is within fifteen feet is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts 2 m short of the intersection behind another car halted 2 m ahead of it in the same lane: a halt in a queue of traffic."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts at the stop line 1 m short of the intersection where a stop sign governs its lane."}],"literals":[{"span":"a1","text":"fifteen feet","value":15,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of object-tracking and vehicle-dynamics recordings"},{"name":"p.queue_halt_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue","source":"queue spacing (jam density) of urban traffic-flow studies"}],"gaps":[{"span":"p4","kind":"operator","proposal":"`Formula.requiredByRuleSet (who : Arg)`: true at an observation where some rule of the set, engaged there for road user `who`, requires of it the conduct it shows there (here a halt), so that the conduct is in compliance with law; false where no engaged rule requires it; unknown where an engaged rule's requirement is unknown. It decides whether a halt is one another law requires (yielding to a pedestrian, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, before a sidewalk when emerging from a driveway, at a railway crossing), which the words except from the prohibition.","nearest":"Formula.rule and Formula.ruleApplies compose one named rule and read its verdict or its engagement: neither ranges over the rules of the set nor says that a rule requires the conduct shown; the device atoms (dev.stop_sign, dev.traffic_signal, dev.governs) carry only the halts a device directs."}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_52_130_A12","law_refs":["LVMC-11-52-130-A12"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"p1","text":"No person shall stop, stand or park a vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"p2","text":"except when necessary to avoid conflict","role":"standard"},{"id":"p3","text":"with other traffic","role":"exception"},{"id":"p4","text":"in compliance with law","role":"exception"},{"id":"p5","text":"or the directions of a police officer","role":"exception"},{"id":"p6","text":"or a traffic control device,","role":"exception"},{"id":"p7","text":"in any of the following places:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"a1","text":"Within twenty feet of any marked crosswalk.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"p1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"\"stop\" here is prohibited, so DEF-NRS-484A-260 applies by its own scope (\"when prohibited, any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\"); standing and parking are halts too, so the three together are any halt: drv.motion.complete_halt (\"The road user is at rest at the observation\"), a state at one observation, not an act over time. \"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole. \"No person\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"p3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"other traffic\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel\"), claimed whole for a road user other than the subject; rel.ahead_behind_in_lane (\"a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane, along the lane direction\") places it ahead of the halted vehicle and rel.surface_gap (\"distance between the nearest points of two bodies\") measures the gap the operationalization bounds; a centre distance would overstate it (rel.centre_distance's not-a-stand-in clause)."},{"span":"p4","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.stop_sign","dev.traffic_signal","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only: the device atoms carry the halts a device directs (read on span p6), not a halt that another law requires of the vehicle (yielding to a pedestrian in the crosswalk, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, at a railway crossing); no atom or operator decides that some engaged rule requires the halt the vehicle makes. The span is a gap."},{"span":"p5","atoms":["dev.human_direction","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Same mapping as the index's \"unless otherwise directed by a Police Officer\": dev.human_direction (\"a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ∈ {police_officer, ...}; indication ∈ {stop, proceed, slow, turn(dir)}\") with role police_officer and indication stop, governing (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies). dev.governs is read as control of that region, not as the place of the halt (its not-a-stand-in clause). \"police officer\" (DEF-NRS-484A-180) is the role police_officer."},{"span":"p6","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.traffic_signal","dev.railway_signal_or_gate","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the directions of ... a traffic control device\" to halt: a stop sign (dev.stop_sign, \"regulatory sign requiring a full halt\"), a yield sign (dev.yield_sign), a traffic signal (dev.traffic_signal) showing circular_red, a red_arrow, flashing_red or circular_yellow, or a railway signal or gate (dev.railway_signal_or_gate) with lights flashing or gate not up, governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). Each device is read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"a1","atoms":["st.crosswalk","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"any marked crosswalk\" (DEF-NRS-484A-065, \"any portion of a highway at an intersection or elsewhere distinctly indicated for pedestrian crossing by lines or other markings on the surface\") is st.crosswalk (\"marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection; marked attribute\") with the marked attribute true: \"marked\" leaves out the unmarked prolongations. \"Within twenty feet of\" is the ground distance from the vehicle's body to it, st.region_geometry (\"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)\"), which anchors the vehicle; occupancy is not read (its not-a-stand-in clause) since the words state a distance."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), has its body within twenty feet (literal 20 ft) of a marked crosswalk: some st.crosswalk region w with the marked attribute and st_region_geometry_distance(subject, w) at most twenty feet. None of the exceptions holds at the observation: no road user o of traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, not the subject) is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a body gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; no police officer's direction to stop (dev.human_direction role police_officer, indication stop) governs a travel region the subject occupies; no stop sign, yield sign, traffic signal showing a red or yellow indication, or flashing railway signal or lowered gate governs (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region); and the halt is not one another law requires (gap on span p4).","obligation":"The subject is not at rest: drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold at the observation.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.queue_halt_gap"],"narrowings":[{"span":"p2","why":"\"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic\" is read only through a road user of traffic ahead of the vehicle in its lane within the queue gap; a halt for crossing traffic that is not ahead in the lane is not read as necessary.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts 3 m short of a marked mid-block crosswalk with no road user ahead of it, no officer and no device governing its lane, and stays at rest; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car drives over the marked crosswalk at 8 m/s without halting."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts 40 m from the nearest marked crosswalk."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A car halts near a marked crosswalk, but the source maps regions without outlines (st.region_geometry absent): whether it is within twenty feet is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts 3 m short of the marked crosswalk because a pedestrian is crossing in its lane 2 m ahead of its front: a road user of traffic ahead within the queue gap."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts before a marked crosswalk at a signal showing circular_red that governs its lane."}],"literals":[{"span":"a1","text":"twenty feet","value":20,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of object-tracking and vehicle-dynamics recordings"},{"name":"p.queue_halt_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue","source":"queue spacing (jam density) of urban traffic-flow studies"}],"gaps":[{"span":"p4","kind":"operator","proposal":"`Formula.requiredByRuleSet (who : Arg)`: true at an observation where some rule of the set, engaged there for road user `who`, requires of it the conduct it shows there (here a halt), so that the conduct is in compliance with law; false where no engaged rule requires it; unknown where an engaged rule's requirement is unknown. It decides whether a halt is one another law requires (yielding to a pedestrian in a crosswalk, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, at a railway crossing), which the words except from the prohibition.","nearest":"Formula.rule and Formula.ruleApplies compose one named rule and read its verdict or its engagement: neither ranges over the rules of the set nor says that a rule requires the conduct shown; the device atoms (dev.stop_sign, dev.traffic_signal, dev.governs) carry only the halts a device directs."}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_52_130_A2","law_refs":["LVMC-11-52-130-A2"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"p1","text":"No person shall stop, stand or park a vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"p2","text":"except when necessary to avoid conflict","role":"standard"},{"id":"p3","text":"with other traffic","role":"exception"},{"id":"p4","text":"in compliance with law","role":"exception"},{"id":"p5","text":"or the directions of a police officer","role":"exception"},{"id":"p6","text":"or a traffic control device,","role":"exception"},{"id":"p7","text":"in any of the following places:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"q1","text":"At any place or in any space adjacent to a curb","role":"condition"},{"id":"q2","text":"which has been designated and posted as a fire lane","role":"condition"},{"id":"q3","text":"pursuant to the City's Fire Code,","role":"reference"},{"id":"q4","text":"whether the vehicle is attended or unattended","role":"condition"},{"id":"q5","text":"and whether the location is on public or private property.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"p1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"\"stop\" here is prohibited, so DEF-NRS-484A-260 applies by its own scope (\"when prohibited, any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\"); standing and parking are halts too, so the three together are any halt: drv.motion.complete_halt (\"The road user is at rest at the observation\"), a state at one observation, not an act over time. \"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole. \"No person\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"p3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"other traffic\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel\"), claimed whole for a road user other than the subject; rel.ahead_behind_in_lane (\"a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane, along the lane direction\") places it ahead of the halted vehicle and rel.surface_gap (\"distance between the nearest points of two bodies\") measures the gap the operationalization bounds; a centre distance would overstate it (rel.centre_distance's not-a-stand-in clause)."},{"span":"p4","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.stop_sign","dev.traffic_signal","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only: the device atoms carry the halts a device directs (read on span p6), not a halt that another law requires of the vehicle (yielding to a pedestrian, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, at a railway crossing); no atom or operator decides that some engaged rule requires the halt the vehicle makes. The span is a gap."},{"span":"p5","atoms":["dev.human_direction","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Same mapping as the index's \"unless otherwise directed by a Police Officer\": dev.human_direction (\"a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ∈ {police_officer, ...}; indication ∈ {stop, proceed, slow, turn(dir)}\") with role police_officer and indication stop, governing (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies). dev.governs is read as control of that region, not as the place of the halt (its not-a-stand-in clause). \"police officer\" (DEF-NRS-484A-180) is the role police_officer."},{"span":"p6","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.traffic_signal","dev.railway_signal_or_gate","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the directions of ... a traffic control device\" to halt: a stop sign (dev.stop_sign, \"regulatory sign requiring a full halt\"), a yield sign (dev.yield_sign), a traffic signal (dev.traffic_signal) showing circular_red, a red_arrow, flashing_red or circular_yellow, or a railway signal or gate (dev.railway_signal_or_gate) with lights flashing or gate not up, governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). Each device is read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"q1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.curb_zone"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"any place or ... any space adjacent to a curb\" of a designated kind is the signed length of curb and the space beside it: st.curb_zone (\"a signed or marked length of curb; kind ∈ {..., fire_lane, ...}\"), with the vehicle's footprint overlapping it, rel.occupies (\"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (... curb zone ...)\"), as the mapping index reads \"a curb or road surface edge which is painted red indicates no parking\"."},{"span":"q2","atoms":["st.curb_zone"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"designated and posted as a fire lane\" is the curb zone's kind fire_lane (st.curb_zone, \"kind ∈ {passenger_loading, ..., fire_lane, no_stopping, no_parking}\"); the designation is a legal status read through the posted zone's presence (observable_reading, status), the zone being the one span q1 anchors."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"q3","why":"The City's Fire Code is outside this corpus; the designation it authorizes is read through the posted fire-lane zone (span q2), so the reference adds nothing the rule can check."},{"span":"q4","why":"Whether the vehicle is attended or not, the prohibition is the same; the halt is read whoever is in it.","scope":"none"},{"span":"q5","why":"Whether the place is on public or private property, the prohibition is the same; the rule reads the posted fire-lane zone wherever the map records it.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), occupies (rel.occupies) a curb zone of kind fire_lane (st.curb_zone). None of the exceptions holds at the observation: no road user o of traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, not the subject) is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a body gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; no police officer's direction to stop (dev.human_direction role police_officer, indication stop) governs a travel region the subject occupies; no stop sign, yield sign, traffic signal showing a red or yellow indication, or flashing railway signal or lowered gate governs (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region); and the halt is not one another law requires (gap on span p4).","obligation":"The subject is not at rest: drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold at the observation.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.queue_halt_gap"],"narrowings":[{"span":"p2","why":"\"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic\" is read only through a road user of traffic ahead of the vehicle in its lane within the queue gap; a halt for crossing traffic that is not ahead in the lane is not read as necessary.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"q2","why":"The designation and posting as a fire lane is a legal status read through the presence of the curb zone of kind fire_lane.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts in a fire_lane curb zone in front of a building, no road user ahead and no device or officer governing its place, and stays at rest; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car drives along the fire_lane curb zone at 5 m/s without halting."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts at a stretch of curb with no curb zone."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A car halts beside a fire_lane zone, but the source does not observe footprint occupancy of regions (rel.occupies absent): whether it is in the zone is unknown.","masked":["rel.occupies"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts in the fire_lane zone where a police officer's direction to stop governs its lane."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of object-tracking and vehicle-dynamics recordings"},{"name":"p.queue_halt_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue","source":"queue spacing (jam density) of urban traffic-flow studies"}],"gaps":[{"span":"p4","kind":"operator","proposal":"`Formula.requiredByRuleSet (who : Arg)`: true at an observation where some rule of the set, engaged there for road user `who`, requires of it the conduct it shows there (here a halt), so that the conduct is in compliance with law; false where no engaged rule requires it; unknown where an engaged rule's requirement is unknown. It decides whether a halt is one another law requires (yielding to a pedestrian, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, at a railway crossing), which the words except from the prohibition.","nearest":"Formula.rule and Formula.ruleApplies compose one named rule and read its verdict or its engagement: neither ranges over the rules of the set nor says that a rule requires the conduct shown; the device atoms (dev.stop_sign, dev.traffic_signal, dev.governs) carry only the halts a device directs."}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_52_130_A4","law_refs":["LVMC-11-52-130-A4"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"p1","text":"No person shall stop, stand or park a vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"p2","text":"except when necessary to avoid conflict","role":"standard"},{"id":"p3","text":"with other traffic","role":"exception"},{"id":"p4","text":"in compliance with law","role":"exception"},{"id":"p5","text":"or the directions of a police officer","role":"exception"},{"id":"p6","text":"or a traffic control device,","role":"exception"},{"id":"p7","text":"in any of the following places:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"h1","text":"Within the following distances of any fire hydrant,","role":"condition"},{"id":"h2","text":"whether or not the location is posted with a sign,","role":"condition"},{"id":"h3","text":"whether or not the adjacent curb or roadway surface is painted red,","role":"condition"},{"id":"h4","text":"and whether the location is on public or private property:","role":"condition"},{"id":"h5","text":"(a) At a location where parallel parking is permitted, fifteen feet;","role":"condition"},{"id":"h6","text":"(b) At a location where angle parking is permitted or no parking is permitted, twenty feet.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"p1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"\"stop\" here is prohibited, so DEF-NRS-484A-260 applies by its own scope (\"when prohibited, any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\"); standing and parking are halts too, so the three together are any halt: drv.motion.complete_halt (\"The road user is at rest at the observation\"), a state at one observation, not an act over time. \"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole. \"No person\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"p3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"other traffic\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel\"), claimed whole for a road user other than the subject; rel.ahead_behind_in_lane (\"a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane, along the lane direction\") places it ahead of the halted vehicle and rel.surface_gap (\"distance between the nearest points of two bodies\") measures the gap the operationalization bounds; a centre distance would overstate it (rel.centre_distance's not-a-stand-in clause)."},{"span":"p4","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.stop_sign","dev.traffic_signal","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only: the device atoms carry the halts a device directs (read on span p6), not a halt that another law requires of the vehicle (yielding to a pedestrian, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, at a railway crossing); no atom or operator decides that some engaged rule requires the halt the vehicle makes. The span is a gap."},{"span":"p5","atoms":["dev.human_direction","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Same mapping as the index's \"unless otherwise directed by a Police Officer\": dev.human_direction (\"a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ∈ {police_officer, ...}; indication ∈ {stop, proceed, slow, turn(dir)}\") with role police_officer and indication stop, governing (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies). dev.governs is read as control of that region, not as the place of the halt (its not-a-stand-in clause). \"police officer\" (DEF-NRS-484A-180) is the role police_officer."},{"span":"p6","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.traffic_signal","dev.railway_signal_or_gate","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the directions of ... a traffic control device\" to halt: a stop sign (dev.stop_sign, \"regulatory sign requiring a full halt\"), a yield sign (dev.yield_sign), a traffic signal (dev.traffic_signal) showing circular_red, a red_arrow, flashing_red or circular_yellow, or a railway signal or gate (dev.railway_signal_or_gate) with lights flashing or gate not up, governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). Each device is read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"h1","atoms":["st.fire_hydrant","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"any fire hydrant\" is st.fire_hydrant (\"a fire hydrant beside the roadway\"), every one of the scene; \"Within the following distances of\" is the ground distance from the vehicle's body to it, st.region_geometry (\"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)\"), which anchors the vehicle; it is not occupancy (its not-a-stand-in clause), since the words state a distance."},{"span":"h5","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","st.parking_space","st.curb_zone","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"(a) selects the smaller stated distance at a location where parallel parking is permitted. Read as every location that is not of kind (b): no angle_parking, no_parking, no_standing or no_stopping regulatory sign (dev.regulatory_sign) governs (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region), the vehicle occupies no marked bay (st.parking_space) whose angle stands clear of zero, and no curb zone (st.curb_zone) of kind no_parking, no_stopping or fire_lane. The two distances are selected by the same evidence, so a location whose evidence is unobserved decides only where both bounds agree."},{"span":"h6","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","st.parking_space","st.curb_zone","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"(b) \"angle parking is permitted\": an angle_parking regulatory sign (dev.regulatory_sign, \"a point regulation by catalogue code ... angle_parking\") governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region), or a marked bay (st.parking_space, \"marked bay for standing or parking; angle attribute\") the vehicle occupies whose angle exceeds the source's angle resolution; \"no parking is permitted\": a no_parking, no_standing or no_stopping regulatory sign governing that region, or a curb zone (st.curb_zone, kind no_parking, no_stopping or fire_lane) the vehicle occupies. Presence of the posted feature is the evidence of the permission or prohibition (status)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"h2","why":"Whether or not the hydrant's location is posted with a sign, the prohibition is the same: the rule reads the hydrant itself.","scope":"none"},{"span":"h3","why":"Whether or not the curb or roadway beside the hydrant is painted red, the prohibition is the same: the rule reads the hydrant itself, not the paint.","scope":"none"},{"span":"h4","why":"Whether the place is on public or private property, the prohibition is the same: the rule reads the hydrant wherever the map records it.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), has its body within the stated distance of a fire hydrant: some st.