t (who : Arg)`: true at an observation where some rule of the set, engaged there for road user `who`, requires of it the conduct it shows there (here a halt), so that the conduct is in compliance with law; false where no engaged rule requires it; unknown where an engaged rule's requirement is unknown. It decides whether a halt is one another law requires (yielding to a pedestrian, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, at a railway crossing), which the words except from the prohibition.","nearest":"Formula.rule and Formula.ruleApplies compose one named rule and read its verdict or its engagement: neither ranges over the rules of the set nor says that a rule requires the conduct shown; the device atoms (dev.stop_sign, dev.traffic_signal, dev.governs) carry only the halts a device directs."},{"span":"e1","kind":"atom","proposal":"`st.sidewalk_elevator_or_chute` | a freight elevator, lift or chute set in a sidewalk, its doors or opening at the sidewalk surface, carried as a region with a reference point and a boundary, so the ground distance and the along-curb offset from a road user to it are read through `st.region_geometry` and `prim.region_offset_along` **Not a stand-in for:** any other sidewalk fixture (`st.obstruction` kind sidewalk_fixture) | local. It decides where a halt is forbidden: in front of the elevator or chute and within the stated space on each side.","nearest":"st.obstruction kind sidewalk_fixture: a fixture on the sidewalk of any kind (a bench, a pole, a newsrack); the kind does not tell a sidewalk elevator or chute from them, so the forbidden place would be read beside every sidewalk fixture."}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
