ies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the directions of ... a traffic control device\" to halt: a stop sign (dev.stop_sign, \"regulatory sign requiring a full halt\"), a yield sign (dev.yield_sign), a traffic signal (dev.traffic_signal) showing circular_red, a red_arrow, flashing_red or circular_yellow, or a railway signal or gate (dev.railway_signal_or_gate) with lights flashing or gate not up, governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). Each device is read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"h1","atoms":["st.fire_hydrant","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"any fire hydrant\" is st.fire_hydrant (\"a fire hydrant beside the roadway\"), every one of the scene; \"Within the following distances of\" is the ground distance from the vehicle's body to it, st.region_geometry (\"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)\"), which anchors the vehicle; it is not occupancy (its not-a-stand-in clause), since the words state a distance."},{"span":"h5","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","st.parking_space","st.curb_zone","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"(a) selects the smaller stated distance at a location where parallel parking is permitted. Read as every location that is not of kind (b): no angle_parking, no_parking, no_standing or no_stopping regulatory sign (dev.regulatory_sign) governs (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region), the vehicle occupies no marked bay (st.parking_space) whose angle stands clear of zero, and no curb zone (st.curb_zone) of kind no_parking, no_stopping or fire_lane. The two distances are selected by the same evidence, so a location whose evidence is unobserved decides only where both bounds agree."},{"span":"h6","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","st.parking_space","st.curb_zone","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"(b) \"angle parking is permitted\": an angle_parking regulatory sign (dev.regulatory_sign, \"a point regulation by catalogue code ... angle_parking\") governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region), or a marked bay (st.parking_space, \"marked bay for standing or parking; angle attribute\") the vehicle occupies whose angle exceeds the source's angle resolution; \"no parking is permitted\": a no_parking, no_standing or no_stopping regulatory sign governing that region, or a curb zone (st.curb_zone, kind no_parking, no_stopping or fire_lane) the vehicle occupies. Presence of the posted feature is the evidence of the permission or prohibition (status)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"h2","why":"Whether or not the hydrant's location is posted with a sign, the prohibition is the same: the rule reads the hydrant itself.","scope":"none"},{"span":"h3","why":"Whether or not the curb or roadway beside the hydrant is painted red, the prohibition is the same: the rule reads the hydrant itself, not the paint.","scope":"none"},{"span":"h4","why":"Whether the place is on public or private property, the prohibition is the same: the rule reads the hydrant wherever the map records it.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), has its body within the stated distance of a fire hydrant: some st.