(dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). Each device is read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"e1","atoms":["st.obstruction","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only: st.obstruction (\"a physical object on or beside the roadway that is not a road user; kind ∈ {..., sidewalk_fixture, ...}\") with kind sidewalk_fixture includes a sidewalk elevator or chute but does not tell it from a bench, a pole or a newsrack, so the prohibited space would be read beside every sidewalk fixture; st.region_geometry (\"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it\") would anchor the vehicle in front of it, within p.curb_frontage_reach of the object across the sidewalk. The span is a gap."},{"span":"e2","atoms":["st.obstruction","prim.region_offset_along","st.lane_direction","st.travel_region","rel.occupies","kin.extent"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"within a space of five feet on each side of such sidewalk elevator or chute\" re-binds the object of span e1 (\"such\") and extends its frontage along the curb by the stated figure on each side: the along-curb offset from the vehicle's reference point to the object, prim.region_offset_along (\"the signed distance (m) from a road user's reference point ... to a structure region ... measured along a carrier's designated direction\"), read on the travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region, st.lane_direction), is in absolute value at most five feet plus half the vehicle's length (kin.extent). The primitive is a geometric quantity only; the object's identity is the gap of span e1."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), stands in front of a sidewalk elevator or chute or within five feet (literal 5 ft) of it on either side: for such an object x (gap: no atom; nearest st.obstruction of kind sidewalk_fixture), the ground distance from the subject's body to x (st_region_geometry_distance) is at most p.curb_frontage_reach, and on a travel region r the subject occupies, the absolute along-carrier offset to x (prim.region_offset_along) is at most five feet plus half the subject's length (kin_extent length). None of the exceptions holds at the observation: no road user o of traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, not the subject) is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a body gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; no police officer's direction to stop (dev.human_direction role police_officer, indication stop) governs a travel region the subject occupies; no stop sign, yield sign, traffic signal showing a red or yellow indication, or flashing railway signal or lowered gate governs (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies; and the halt is not one another law requires (gap on span p4).","obligation":"The subject is not at rest: drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold at the observation.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.queue_halt_gap","p.curb_frontage_reach"],"narrowings":[{"span":"p2","why":"\"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic\" is read only through a road user of traffic ahead of the vehicle in its lane within the queue gap; a halt for crossing traffic that is not ahead in the lane is not read as necessary.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios