ld sign (dev.yield_sign), a traffic signal (dev.traffic_signal) showing circular_red, a red_arrow, flashing_red or circular_yellow, or a railway signal or gate (dev.railway_signal_or_gate) with lights flashing or gate not up, governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). Each device is read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"q1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.curb_zone"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"any place or ... any space adjacent to a curb\" of a designated kind is the signed length of curb and the space beside it: st.curb_zone (\"a signed or marked length of curb; kind ∈ {..., fire_lane, ...}\"), with the vehicle's footprint overlapping it, rel.occupies (\"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (... curb zone ...)\"), as the mapping index reads \"a curb or road surface edge which is painted red indicates no parking\"."},{"span":"q2","atoms":["st.curb_zone"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"designated and posted as a fire lane\" is the curb zone's kind fire_lane (st.curb_zone, \"kind ∈ {passenger_loading, ..., fire_lane, no_stopping, no_parking}\"); the designation is a legal status read through the posted zone's presence (observable_reading, status), the zone being the one span q1 anchors."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"q3","why":"The City's Fire Code is outside this corpus; the designation it authorizes is read through the posted fire-lane zone (span q2), so the reference adds nothing the rule can check."},{"span":"q4","why":"Whether the vehicle is attended or not, the prohibition is the same; the halt is read whoever is in it.","scope":"none"},{"span":"q5","why":"Whether the place is on public or private property, the prohibition is the same; the rule reads the posted fire-lane zone wherever the map records it.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), occupies (rel.occupies) a curb zone of kind fire_lane (st.curb_zone). None of the exceptions holds at the observation: no road user o of traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, not the subject) is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a body gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; no police officer's direction to stop (dev.human_direction role police_officer, indication stop) governs a travel region the subject occupies; no stop sign, yield sign, traffic signal showing a red or yellow indication, or flashing railway signal or lowered gate governs (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region); and the halt is not one another law requires (gap on span p4).","obligation":"The subject is not at rest: drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold at the observation.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.queue_halt_gap"],"narrowings":[{"span":"p2","why":"\"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic\" is read only through a road user of traffic ahead of the vehicle in its lane within the queue gap; a halt for crossing traffic that is not ahead in the lane is not read as necessary.","kind":"reading"},{"span":"q2","why":"The designation and posting as a fire lane is a legal status read through the presence of the curb zone of kind fire_lane.","kind":"observable_reading","category":"status"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts in a fire_lane curb zone in front of a building, no road user ahead and no device or officer governing its place, and stays at rest; no other road user is in the scene."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car drives along the fire_lane curb zone at 5 m/s without halting."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts at a stretch of curb with no curb zone."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A car halts beside a fire_lane zone, but the source does not observe footprint occupancy of regions (rel.occupies absent): whether it is in the zone is unknown.","masked":["rel.occupies"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts in the fire_lane zone where a police officer's direction to stop governs its lane."}],"literals":[],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of object-tracking and vehicle-dynamics recordings"},{"name":"p.queue_halt_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue","source":"queue spacing (jam density) of urban traffic-flow studies"}],"gaps":[{"span":"p4","kind":"operator","proposal":"`Formula.requiredByRuleSet (who : Arg)`: true at an observation where some rule of the set, engaged there for road user `who`, requires of it the conduct it shows there (here a halt), so that the conduct is in compliance with law; false where no engaged rule requires it; unknown where an engaged rule's requirement is unknown. It decides whether a halt is one another law requires (yielding to a pedestrian, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, at a railway crossing), which the words except from the prohibition.","nearest":"Formula.rule and Formula.ruleApplies compose one named rule and read its verdict or its engagement: neither ranges over the rules of the set nor says that a rule requires the conduct shown; the device atoms (dev.stop_sign, dev.traffic_signal, dev.governs) carry only the halts a device directs."}],"gap_resolutions":[]}
{"node_id":"LVMC_11_52_130_A4","law_refs":["LVMC-11-52-130-A4"],"subject":{"binder":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]},"segmentation":[{"id":"p1","text":"No person shall stop, stand or park a vehicle","role":"obligation"},{"id":"p2","text":"except when necessary to avoid conflict","role":"standard"},{"id":"p3","text":"with other traffic","role":"exception"},{"id":"p4","text":"in compliance with law","role":"exception"},{"id":"p5","text":"or the directions of a police officer","role":"exception"},{"id":"p6","text":"or a traffic control device,","role":"exception"},{"id":"p7","text":"in any of the following places:","role":"boilerplate"},{"id":"h1","text":"Within the following distances of any fire hydrant,","role":"condition"},{"id":"h2","text":"whether or not the location is posted with a sign,","role":"condition"},{"id":"h3","text":"whether or not the adjacent curb or roadway surface is painted red,","role":"condition"},{"id":"h4","text":"and whether the location is on public or private property:","role":"condition"},{"id":"h5","text":"(a) At a location where parallel parking is permitted, fifteen feet;","role":"condition"},{"id":"h6","text":"(b) At a location where angle parking is permitted or no parking is permitted, twenty feet.","role":"condition"}],"elements":[{"span":"p1","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"],"derived":["drv.motion.complete_halt"],"justification":"\"stop\" here is prohibited, so DEF-NRS-484A-260 applies by its own scope (\"when prohibited, any halting, even momentarily, of a vehicle, whether occupied or not\"); standing and parking are halts too, so the three together are any halt: drv.motion.complete_halt (\"The road user is at rest at the observation\"), a state at one observation, not an act over time. \"a vehicle\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle, claimed whole. \"No person\" is read through the vehicle's controlled motion."},{"span":"p3","atoms":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic","rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"other traffic\" is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic (\"pedestrians, ridden or herded animals, vehicles and other conveyances either singly or together using any highway for purposes of travel\"), claimed whole for a road user other than the subject; rel.ahead_behind_in_lane (\"a is ahead of / behind b in the same lane, along the lane direction\") places it ahead of the halted vehicle and rel.surface_gap (\"distance between the nearest points of two bodies\") measures the gap the operationalization bounds; a centre distance would overstate it (rel.centre_distance's not-a-stand-in clause)."},{"span":"p4","atoms":["dev.governs","dev.stop_sign","dev.traffic_signal","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Nearest atoms only: the device atoms carry the halts a device directs (read on span p6), not a halt that another law requires of the vehicle (yielding to a pedestrian, stopping for a school bus or an emergency vehicle, at a railway crossing); no atom or operator decides that some engaged rule requires the halt the vehicle makes. The span is a gap."},{"span":"p5","atoms":["dev.human_direction","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"Same mapping as the index's \"unless otherwise directed by a Police Officer\": dev.human_direction (\"a person directing traffic and the direction given; role ∈ {police_officer, ...}; indication ∈ {stop, proceed, slow, turn(dir)}\") with role police_officer and indication stop, governing (dev.governs) a travel region (st.travel_region) the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies). dev.governs is read as control of that region, not as the place of the halt (its not-a-stand-in clause). \"police officer\" (DEF-NRS-484A-180) is the role police_officer."},{"span":"p6","atoms":["dev.stop_sign","dev.yield_sign","dev.traffic_signal","dev.railway_signal_or_gate","dev.governs","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"the directions of ... a traffic control device\" to halt: a stop sign (dev.stop_sign, \"regulatory sign requiring a full halt\"), a yield sign (dev.yield_sign), a traffic signal (dev.traffic_signal) showing circular_red, a red_arrow, flashing_red or circular_yellow, or a railway signal or gate (dev.railway_signal_or_gate) with lights flashing or gate not up, governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). Each device is read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"h1","atoms":["st.fire_hydrant","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"any fire hydrant\" is st.fire_hydrant (\"a fire hydrant beside the roadway\"), every one of the scene; \"Within the following distances of\" is the ground distance from the vehicle's body to it, st.region_geometry (\"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)\"), which anchors the vehicle; it is not occupancy (its not-a-stand-in clause), since the words state a distance."},{"span":"h5","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","st.parking_space","st.curb_zone","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"(a) selects the smaller stated distance at a location where parallel parking is permitted. Read as every location that is not of kind (b): no angle_parking, no_parking, no_standing or no_stopping regulatory sign (dev.regulatory_sign) governs (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region), the vehicle occupies no marked bay (st.parking_space) whose angle stands clear of zero, and no curb zone (st.curb_zone) of kind no_parking, no_stopping or fire_lane. The two distances are selected by the same evidence, so a location whose evidence is unobserved decides only where both bounds agree."},{"span":"h6","atoms":["dev.regulatory_sign","dev.governs","st.parking_space","st.curb_zone","rel.occupies","st.travel_region"],"derived":[],"justification":"(b) \"angle parking is permitted\": an angle_parking regulatory sign (dev.regulatory_sign, \"a point regulation by catalogue code ... angle_parking\") governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region), or a marked bay (st.parking_space, \"marked bay for standing or parking; angle attribute\") the vehicle occupies whose angle exceeds the source's angle resolution; \"no parking is permitted\": a no_parking, no_standing or no_stopping regulatory sign governing that region, or a curb zone (st.curb_zone, kind no_parking, no_stopping or fire_lane) the vehicle occupies. Presence of the posted feature is the evidence of the permission or prohibition (status)."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"h2","why":"Whether or not the hydrant's location is posted with a sign, the prohibition is the same: the rule reads the hydrant itself.","scope":"none"},{"span":"h3","why":"Whether or not the curb or roadway beside the hydrant is painted red, the prohibition is the same: the rule reads the hydrant itself, not the paint.","scope":"none"},{"span":"h4","why":"Whether the place is on public or private property, the prohibition is the same: the rule reads the hydrant wherever the map records it.","scope":"none"}],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), has its body within the stated distance of a fire hydrant: some st.fire_hydrant region f with st_region_geometry_distance(subject, f) at most the bound Term.cond(B, twenty feet, fifteen feet) (literals 20 ft and 15 ft), where B holds at a location where angle parking or no parking is permitted: an angle_parking, no_parking, no_standing or no_stopping regulatory sign (dev.regulatory_sign) governs (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region), or the subject occupies a parking space (st.parking_space) whose angle in absolute value exceeds p.parking_space_angle_resolution, or a curb zone (st.curb_zone) of kind no_parking, no_stopping or fire_lane. None of the exceptions holds at the observation: no road user o of traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, not the subject) is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a body gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; no police officer's direction to stop (dev.human_direction role police_officer, indication stop) governs a travel region the subject occupies; no stop sign, yield sign, traffic signal showing a red or yellow indication, or flashing railway signal or lowered gate governs (dev.governs) a travel region the subject occupies; and the halt is not one another law requires (gap on span p4).","obligation":"The subject is not at rest: drv.motion.complete_halt(subject; speed_tol = p.halt_speed_tolerance) does not hold at the observation.","params":["p.halt_speed_tolerance","p.queue_halt_gap","p.parking_space_angle_resolution"],"narrowings":[{"span":"p2","why":"\"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic\" is read only through a road user of traffic ahead of the vehicle in its lane within the queue gap; a halt for crossing traffic that is not ahead in the lane is not read as necessary.","kind":"reading"}],"scenarios":[{"name":"forbid","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts parallel to the curb with its body 2 m from a fire hydrant, at a curb with no sign and no angled bay, and stays at rest; no other road user and no device is in the scene."},{"name":"permit","expected":"compliant","narrative":"A car drives past the fire hydrant at 6 m/s, its body 1.5 m from it, without halting."},{"name":"idle","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts parallel to the curb with its body 10 m from the nearest hydrant, where no angle-parking or no-parking sign or zone applies: beyond fifteen feet."},{"name":"blind","expected":"unknown","narrative":"A car halts near a fire hydrant, but the source maps regions without outlines (st.region_geometry absent): its distance to the hydrant is unknown.","masked":["st.region_geometry"]},{"name":"branch_1","expected":"violated","narrative":"A car halts in an angled bay (angle 60 degrees) with its body 5.5 m from a fire hydrant: beyond fifteen feet but within twenty, the bound of an angle-parking location."},{"name":"branch_2","expected":"not_applicable","narrative":"A car halts parallel to the curb with its body 5.5 m from a hydrant where no angle-parking or no-parking sign or zone applies: beyond fifteen feet."}],"literals":[{"span":"h5","text":"fifteen feet","value":15,"unit":"ft"},{"span":"h6","text":"twenty feet","value":20,"unit":"ft"}],"param_proposals":[{"name":"p.halt_speed_tolerance","unit":"m/s","value":0.1,"convention":"the speed at or below which a sampled speed counts as no movement: the source's speed resolution","source":"speed resolution of object-tracking and vehicle-dynamics recordings"},{"name":"p.queue_halt_gap","unit":"m","value":5.0,"convention":"the gap between bodies to a road user ahead in the same lane within which a halt is a halt behind other traffic: the spacing of halted vehicles in a queue","source":"queue spacing (jam density) of urban traffic-flow studies"},{"name":"p.parking_space_angle_resolution","unit":"deg","value":5.0,"convention":"the bay angle at or below which a mapped parking bay counts as parallel to the curb rather than angled: the source's angle resolution for mapped bays","source"