read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"a1","atoms":["st.crosswalk","st.region_geometry"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"any marked crosswalk\" (DEF-NRS-484A-065, \"any portion of a highway at an intersection or elsewhere distinctly indicated for pedestrian crossing by lines or other markings on the surface\") is st.crosswalk (\"marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection; marked attribute\") with the marked attribute true: \"marked\" leaves out the unmarked prolongations. \"Within twenty feet of\" is the ground distance from the vehicle's body to it, st.region_geometry (\"the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it (zero when they overlap)\"), which anchors the vehicle; occupancy is not read (its not-a-stand-in clause) since the words state a distance."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[],"binders":[{"name":"subject","class_elements":["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}],"applicability":"The subject, a vehicle (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle), has its body within twenty feet (literal 20 ft) of a marked crosswalk: some st.crosswalk region w with the marked attribute and st_region_geometry_distance(subject, w) at most twenty feet. None of the exceptions holds at the observation: no road user o of traffic (ru.aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic, not the subject) is ahead of the subject in the same lane (rel.ahead_behind_in_lane) with a body gap (rel.surface_gap) at most p.queue_halt_gap; no police officer's direction to stop (de