ld sign (dev.yield_sign), a traffic signal (dev.traffic_signal) showing circular_red, a red_arrow, flashing_red or circular_yellow, or a railway signal or gate (dev.railway_signal_or_gate) with lights flashing or gate not up, governing (dev.governs) a travel region the vehicle occupies (rel.occupies, st.travel_region). Each device is read by its own state; a sign is not a signal. Its official status is presumed from its presence."},{"span":"q1","atoms":["rel.occupies","st.curb_zone"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"any place or ... any space adjacent to a curb\" of a designated kind is the signed length of curb and the space beside it: st.curb_zone (\"a signed or marked length of curb; kind ∈ {..., fire_lane, ...}\"), with the vehicle's footprint overlapping it, rel.occupies (\"a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region (... curb zone ...)\"), as the mapping index reads \"a curb or road surface edge which is painted red indicates no parking\"."},{"span":"q2","atoms":["st.curb_zone"],"derived":[],"justification":"\"designated and posted as a fire lane\" is the curb zone's kind fire_lane (st.curb_zone, \"kind ∈ {passenger_loading, ..., fire_lane, no_stopping, no_parking}\"); the designation is a legal status read through the posted zone's presence (observable_reading, status), the zone being the one span q1 anchors."}],"operationalizations":[{"span":"p2","standard":"necessary to avoid conflict with other traffic","concepts":["rel.ahead_behind_in_lane","rel.surface_gap"],"params":["p.queue_halt_gap"],"convention":"queue spacing: a halt with a road user of traffic ahead in the same lane within the body gap of halted vehicles in a queue is a halt the traffic ahead makes necessary","surrogate":false}],"assumptions":[],"intentions":[],"compositions":[],"residues":[{"span":"q3","why":"The City's Fire Code is outside this corpus; the designation it authorizes is read through the posted fire-lane zone (span q2), so the reference adds nothing the rule can check."},{"span